      "title": "DR. MAREN'S NOTES",
      "text": "The stone is not a mineral. Cut thin, it is a lens. Through it the room behind looks the same, but something stands in it that is not in the room. It is always standing a little nearer than the last time you looked."
    },
    {
      "x": 2,
      "y": 21,
      "dx": 0,
      "dy": -1,
      "title": "DR. MAREN'S LAST NOTE",
      "text": "The Directorate wants a ring of the stone, twenty metres across, in the sanctum. I have told them that a lens that size will not show us the other side. It will show the other side us. They said that was the point."
    }
